  "direction": "How much epistasis can simple sequence-to-fitness models absorb? On simulated NK fitness landscapes (sequence length 15 to 20, alphabet size 4 to 20, K from 0 to 4) compare an additive (one-hot ridge) model, a pairwise-epistasis model, a small CNN and a small MLP, trained on a few hundred to a few thousand measured variants. Measure Spearman correlation on held-out variants and the success of a greedy design step proposing higher-fitness sequences. State clearly that the landscapes are simulated.",
